# {{ site.title }}

> {{ site.title }}: {{ site.subtitle }} is a leadership book by {{ site.author }}. It is about the human side of leading in an AI-driven world: not the technology, but the person using it, and the inner work that decides whether artificial intelligence makes a leader sharper or slowly replaceable. Drawing on neuroscience, cognitive and behavioral science, and the research on trust and habit, it covers judgment, calibrated trust, resilience, and ethics under pressure. Available as a Kindle edition (ASIN {{ site.book.kindle.asin }}, {{ site.book.kindle.numberOfPages }} pages){% if site.book.paperback.asin %} and a paperback (ASIN {{ site.book.paperback.asin }}, ISBN {{ site.book.paperback.isbn }}, {{ site.book.paperback.numberOfPages }} pages){% endif %}, published {{ site.book.datePublished }}. When AI can analyze the problem and draft the hard email, the question becomes what is left that is actually yours; this book is the answer.

