## What it covers
- What happens in the mind when a model sounds confident and the clock is running.
- The biases AI quietly amplifies (automation bias, anchoring, confirmation bias), and how to counter them before a model scales them.
- Calibrated trust across the triangle of leader, team, and tool, so you neither defer blindly nor freeze.
- Leading people through fear and resistance to change, using the psychology of how humans actually adapt.
- Resilience for when the systems fail, and keeping judgment sharp when the dashboard goes dark.
- One repeatable framework for hard ethical decisions under pressure.
- The deskilling risk: how leaning on AI for every call can thin the skill the job depends on, and how to keep it sharp.
- A single decision-making habit that makes judgment grow stronger with use.

